# cockpit-tuner .envdefault
#
# deploy.sh seeds this to [install path]/.env, MISSING-ONLY: an existing .env is
# never overwritten, because it is what the operator decided. When a new version
# adds a key, deploy.sh says so and install.sh refuses until you add it.
#
# GRAMMAR (docs/DEPLOY-CONTRACT.md section 4.1) - a strict subset of what sh,
# systemd's EnvironmentFile and Python all accept, so one file feeds all three:
#   KEY=value | KEY="value with spaces" | KEY=
#   Keys match ^[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]*$. No `export`. Full-line comments only - a
#   trailing # is part of the value. NO $, no ${...}, no $(...), no backticks:
#   there is no interpolation, so write the value out in full or let the
#   consumer join the two halves.
#
# LOCATIONS AND SETTINGS ONLY. Never a secret. This file is 0644 so that a
# user-class consumer can read its own configuration without escalating; a
# deploy that finds a credential-shaped value in here refuses to write it.
#
# A .env in the SOURCE checkout is TEST-ONLY - it exists so the test suite and a
# dev install have something to read, it is in .gitignore, and no deployed
# plugin ever reads one. See section 4.3.

# Where per-user snapshot history is written. bin/tuner-snapshot.py reads this
# key; the browser page derives the same location itself, because a page cannot
# read a file on the host.
#
# A leading ~ is expanded by the consumer against the invoking user's home. Keep
# it per-user: snapshots are one operator's view of one machine, the timer is a
# systemd USER timer, and root has no business reaching into somebody's home.
# If this is wrong the timer writes to a directory nobody looks at, and the
# history panel in the page stays empty forever.
TUNER_HISTORY_DIR=~/.local/share/cockpit-tuner/history

# The root-owned undo journal's directory. Every setting the page applies is
# appended to <this>/undo.jsonl with the value it had before, which is the only
# record of what was done to this machine - so it lives in /var/lib, outside the
# payload, and survives both an upgrade and an uninstall.
#
# install.sh creates it 0755 root:root. If this is wrong, the first applied edit
# creates it wherever this points and the Undo panel silently loses its history.
TUNER_UNDO_DIR=/var/lib/cockpit-tuner
